// test-execution
// test-adr: 010
// Negative control for #1508, in two directions at once.
//
// 1. THE 2-HOP FILE DEFINES NOTHING THIS ENTRY NEEDS. `leaf.cnx` sits in this
//    fixture's include closure exactly as it does for `entry.test.cnx`, but
//    nothing here calls `leafValue`. Linking it anyway must be harmless. If the
//    closure fix had been written as "link every `.c` in the directory" this
//    would still pass -- which is why it is not the only control.
//
// 2. THIS FIXTURE AND `entry.test.cnx` EACH DEFINE `main`, IN ONE DIRECTORY.
//    That is the half that actually discriminates. A link step that took the
//    directory rather than the closure would hand each fixture the other's
//    object and fail on `multiple definition of 'main'`. Linking the closure
//    gives each fixture only what it includes, so both pass.
//
//    This is the shape the issue's acceptance asks for: the fix must not be
//    "link every `.c` in the directory", because that would also link a file
//    whose symbol is genuinely missing and hide the very defect the harness is
//    supposed to report.
#include "mid.cnx"

u32 main() {
    u32 v <- midOnly();
    if (v != 7) return 1;
    return 0;
}
